# THE ROPE MATERIAL: locs, dreadlocks, cornrows and bantu knots.
#
# `transparent False`, and that is the point of it. The sheet this wears used to
# be alpha-cut like every other strand texture here, which meant 41% of each
# rope's surface was HOLES. On a card or a shell those holes are the gaps
# between hairs at the silhouette and cutting them is the whole technique; on a
# rope they make the thing see-through, and a head of forty-one of them read as
# stacked sheets of cellophane. Lumpy geometry could not fix that, because it
# was never the geometry.
#
# `tools/make_hair_alpha.py` now writes this sheet SOLID (`solid=True`): the
# strand pattern shades the rope instead of perforating it, which is what a
# photograph of a loc shows -- fibre running along it, not light through it.
# The swept styles' material: cornrows, locs and bantu knots.
#
# A SEPARATE SHEET FROM `hair.mhmat`, and the split is measured rather than
# stylistic. `hair_strands.png` carries 52 strands, which is right for geometry
# with many samples across `u` -- the afro's cap and a coil's card. These three
# are swept TUBES of six or seven facets around, so 52 strands lands about
# eight to a facet and aliases: rendered, cornrows nearly vanished, locs read
# as threads, the knots speckled. `hair_tube_strands.png` carries seven, about
# one per facet, which is what the original 8-strand sheet was sized for.
#
# Everything else matches `hair.mhmat`, so the three styles still read as the
# same head of hair as the afro beside them.
name Hair
tag MakeHuman™
ambientColor 0.04 0.03 0.02
diffuseColor 0.28 0.19 0.13
specularColor 0.6 0.6 0.6
shininess 0.3
opacity 1.0
transparent False
diffuseTexture ../hair_tube_strands.png
backfaceCull True
castShadows True
receiveShadows True
shader data/shaders/glsl/litsphere
